nw nx hl bl">Inheritance is a mechanism wherein a new class (known as the child or subclass) derives properties and behaviors (fields and methods) from an existing class (known as the parent or superclass). This allows for the reuse of code and the creation of a hierarchical relationship between classes.</p><p id="07ef" class="pw-post-body-paragraph na nb hs nc b nd ne nf ng nh ni nj nk nl nm nn no np nq nr ns nt nu nv nw nx hl bl">Key Terminologies: Parent Class and Child Class</p><ul class=""><li id="e727" class="na nb hs nc b nd ne nf ng nh ni nj nk nl nm nn no np nq nr ns nt nu nv nw nx ny nz oa bl">Parent Class (Superclass): The class whose properties and methods are inherited by another class.</li><li id="d656" class="na nb hs nc b nd ob nf ng nh oc nj nk nl od nn no np oe nr ns nt of nv nw nx ny nz oa bl">Child Class (Subclass): The class that inherits properties and methods from the parent class.</li></ul><p id="9cfd" class="pw-post-body-paragraph na nb hs nc b nd ne nf ng nh ni nj nk nl nm nn no np nq nr ns nt nu nv nw nx hl bl">How Inheritance Works in Java</p><p id="454d" class="pw-post-body-paragraph na nb hs nc b nd ne nf ng nh ni nj nk nl nm nn no np nq nr ns nt nu nv nw nx hl bl">Syntax of Inheritance: In Java, inheritance is implemented using the extends keyword.</p><figure class="oj ok ol om on oo og oh paragraph-image"><div role="button" tabindex="0" class="op oq fz or bi os"><span class="ge gf gg ao gh gi gj fs gk speechify-ignore">Press enter or click to view image in full size</span><div class="og oh oi"><picture><source srcset="https://miro.medium.com/v2/resize:fit:640/format:webp/0*sUfuWNN2p23_vBnm 640w, https://miro.medium.com/v2/resize:fit:720/format:webp/0*sUfuWNN2p23_vBnm 720w, https://miro.medium.com/v2/resize:fit:750/format:webp/0*sUfuWNN2p23_vBnm 750w, https://miro.medium.com/v2/resize:fit:786/format:webp/0*sUfuWNN2p23_vBnm 786w, https://miro.medium.com/v2/resize:fit:828/format:webp/0*sUfuWNN2p23_vBnm 828w, https://miro.medium.com/v2/re